# Test data

The `.html` fixtures in this directory are pruned snapshots of the live
CourtReserve "My Reservations" page (`app.courtreserve.com/Online/Bookings/List/7031`).

## How they were created

1. **Saved from live data.** Log in to CourtReserve in a real Chromium, open the
   bookings list, and use the browser's "Save page as..." to capture the page
   as an MHTML file (`.mhtml`). The raw captures are gitignored and sit beside
   the fixtures here, several MB each.

2. **Prune to reduce size.** `recapture.ts` does it:

   ```
   npx tsx test/data/recapture.ts <capture.mhtml> [anchor] [out.html] [tag]
   ```

   It decodes the quoted-printable `text/html` part, slices from `anchor`
   (default `data-testid="booking-tabs"`) through that element's matching
   closing tag, and wraps the result in a minimal HTML shell:

   ```html
   <!DOCTYPE html>
   <html lang="en">
   <head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Booking List | powered by CourtReserve</title></head>
   <body>
   ...subtree...
   </body>
   </html>
   ```

   This shrinks each fixture from ~4.8 MB to a few KB. The markup inside is
   byte-for-byte as the site served it; only the surrounding CSS, images, and
   scripts are removed. `tag` overrides which element is sliced — needed when
   the anchor is not a `<div>` (`data-testid="member-table"` is on a `<table>`)
   or carries no testid at all (`class="header-nav`).

   Two things the script does not do: the committed fixtures are hand-trimmed
   subsets of the subtree, not byte-exact output, and a live capture contains
   real member names, so check for those before committing. The `/recapture`
   command (`.opencode/command/recapture.md`) walks the whole procedure.

## Fixtures

- `one-booking-two-people.html` — one editable booking ("Edit Reservation").
- `no-booking.html` — no booking cards.
- `booking-by-other-people.html` — three bookings: one added by someone else
  ("Details" button, not editable) and two owned by the current user
  ("Edit Reservation" button).
- `not-logged-in.html` — the header nav from the unauthenticated portal home
  (`/Online/Portal/Index/7031`), which renders the `LOG IN` link to
  `/Online/Account/LogIn/7031`. Used to test login-state detection.
- `login-page.html` — the login form from `/Online/Account/LogIn/7031`:
  `input[name="email"]`, `input[name="password"]`, and the
  `button[data-testid="Continue"]` submit. Used to test credential login.
- `adding-player/` — the edit-reservation flow read by `players.test.ts`:
  `edit-modal.html`, `player-options.html`, `no-player-options.html`,
  `player-added.html`, `confirm-dialog.html`, `reservation-confirmed.html`,
  `reservation-detail.html`. (`two-bookings.html` is not read by any test.)
- `removing-player/` — `modal-player-list.html` and `modal-player-removed.html`,
  the `data-testid="member-table"` grid before and after a removal.
- `reserving-courts/` — captures of the book-a-court flow. Gitignored, no
  functional test reads them; reference only.

## Caveats

Because the CSS is gone, the fixtures have no realistic layout. Assertions on
geometry (bounding boxes, scrolling, hover targets) will not match production;
only DOM structure and text are faithful.
